ds: `pickle.load`, `torch.load`, `joblib.load`, `.pkl`, `.pt`, `.bin` files. 2) Check the loader refuses these formats unless an approved exception and scan are recorded. 3) Answer no if any pickle-based load runs without that check.\n115\t\n116\t**Reviewer's evidence:** release/manifest.json:32 — \"\"adapter\": null,\"\n117\t\n118\t**Reviewer's note:** No pickle model loads\n119\t\n120\t`release/manifest.json` lines 20–44 (cited lines marked >):\n121\t```\n122\t  20        \"requestedId\": \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\n123\t  21        \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n124\t  22        \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n125\t  23        \"adapter\": null,\n126\t  24        \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n127\t  25      },\n128\t  26      {\n129\t  27        \"role\": \"intent_classifier\",\n130\t  28        \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n131\t  29        \"requestedId\": \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\n132\t  30        \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n133\t  31        \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n134\t  32>       \"adapter\": null,\n135\t  33        \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n136\t  34      }\n137\t  35    ],\n138\t  36    \"tools\": {\n139\t  37      \"allowlist\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\",\n140\t  38      \"mcpServers\": [\n141\t  39        {\n142\t  40          \"id\": \"ehr\",\n143\t  41          \"url\": \"https://ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example/mcp\",\n144\t  42          \"tlsCertSha256\": \"1f6a9c3e5b7d9f1a3c5e7b9d1f3a5c7e9b1d3f5a7c9e1b3d5f7a9c1e3b5d7f9a\",\n145\t  43          \"owner\": \"ehr-integrations@northbay-clinics.example\"\n146\t  44        }\n147\t```\n148\t\n149\t## C05.5\n150\t\n151\t**Check:** The model version the provider or runtime reports serving is recorded separately from the requested model name.\n152\t\n153\t**How to verify:** 1) Find model call sites and their response handling. 2) Check the served version from the response or runtime (for example the response `model` field) is stored in its own field. 3) Answer no if only the requested name is recorded, or the served field is filled with the requested value.\n154\t\n155\t**Reviewer's evidence:** src/agent/loop.ts:71 — \"servedModel: res.model,\"\n156\t\n157\t**Reviewer's note:** Served model recorded separately\n158\t\n159\t`src/agent/loop.ts` lines 59–83 (cited lines marked >):\n160\t```\n161\t  59        const req = { model: AGENT_MODEL, system, tools, messages };\n162\t  60        const pre = await measureBeforeCall(anthropic, req, budget.signal);\n163\t  61        const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\n164\t  62        const contextSize = completeFromUsage(pre, res.usage);\n165\t  63        await budget.recordUsage(res.usage, AGENT_MODEL);\n166\t  64  \n167\t  65        const toolUses = res.content.filter((b): b is Anthropic.ToolUseBlock => b.type === \"tool_use\");\n168\t  66        await audit.record({\n169\t  67          ...ident(),\n170\t  68          event: \"model.decision\",\n171\t  69          context: contextSize,\n172\t  70          detail: {\n173\t  71>           servedModel: res.model,\n174\t  72            stopReason: res.stop_reason,\n175\t  73            proposed: toolUses.map((t) => ({ id: t.id, name: t.name })),\n176\t  74            span: spanAttributes(contextSize),\n177\t  75          },\n178\t  76        });\n179\t  77  \n180\t  78        if (res.stop_reason !== \"tool_use\" || toolUses.length === 0) {\n181\t  79          const text = res.content\n182\t  80            .filter((b): b is Anthropic.TextBlock => b.type === \"text\")\n183\t  81            .map((b) => b.text)\n184\t  82            .join(\"\\n\")\n185\t  83            .slice(0, 320);\n186\t```\n187\t\n188\t## Your answer\n189\t\n190\tWrite this JSON to C05.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"C05\"):\n191\t```json\n192\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n193\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"C05.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n194\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n195\t```\n196\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n197\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e7e8489-61b2-450b-8567-0516c1d8b7ec","uuid":"007c6f08-743a-43bb-b20c-c09d79479e05","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:51:24.540Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-ypxvqv9o/sheet.md","content":"# Gap hunt: C05 — Control dependency, model, and training changes\n\nA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\ncheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\nlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n  Quote that line;\n- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\n**The requirement for C05:** Pin dependency versions. Where supported, also pin each model's base version, checkpoint or weights, and fine-tune or adapt